<div class="path-head"><p class="featured-region">Reading path · 9 stops</p><h1 class="path-title">Women Who Ruled</h1><p class="path-tagline">Nine rulers who held power in their own right, from the Nile to the Forbidden City.</p><p class="path-intro">In most ages the rules said a woman could not rule, and in every age some did anyway. This path crosses four millennia of them: a pharaoh who wore the false beard, warrior queens who fought Rome, the only woman to found a Chinese dynasty, an African queen who out-negotiated an empire, and the empresses who steered Russia and China through their most dangerous centuries.</p><p class="path-types">Suits <a href="/start">the Chronicler</a></p></div>
<ol class="path-steps"><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/hatshepsut"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hatshepsut.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">1 · Encyclopedia · Person · c. 1479–1458 BCE</span><span class="path-step-name">Hatshepsut</span><span class="path-step-why">The pharaoh who ruled Egypt for two decades and built like a king.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/cleopatra-vii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cleopatra-vii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">2 · Encyclopedia · Person · r. 51–30 BCE</span><span class="path-step-name">Cleopatra VII</span><span class="path-step-why">The last Ptolemy, who played Rome's strongmen against each other for twenty years.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/boudica"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boudica.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">3 · Encyclopedia · Person · d. 60 or 61</span><span class="path-step-name">Boudica</span><span class="path-step-why">The Iceni queen whose revolt burned Roman London.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/zenobia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zenobia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">4 · Encyclopedia · Person · c. 240–after 274</span><span class="path-step-name">Zenobia</span><span class="path-step-why">The queen of Palmyra who carved an empire from Rome's east.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/wu-zetian"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wu-zetian.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">5 · Encyclopedia · Person · r. 690–705</span><span class="path-step-name">Wu Zetian</span><span class="path-step-why">The only woman to rule China as emperor in her own name.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/seondeok-of-silla"><span class="path-step-ph">6</span><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">6 · Encyclopedia · Person · d. 647</span><span class="path-step-name">Seondeok of Silla</span><span class="path-step-why">Korea's first reigning queen, patron of scholars and stargazers.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/njinga-of-ndongo-and-matamba"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/njinga-of-ndongo-and-matamba.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">7 · Encyclopedia · Person · c. 1583–1663</span><span class="path-step-name">Njinga of Ndongo and Matamba</span><span class="path-step-why">The queen who fought and out-bargained the Portuguese for forty years.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">8 · Encyclopedia · Person · 1533–1603</span><span class="path-step-name">Elizabeth I</span><span class="path-step-why">Gloriana: the unmarried queen who made a weak realm a power.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-the-great"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/catherine-the-great.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">9 · Encyclopedia · Person</span><span class="path-step-name">Catherine the Great</span><span class="path-step-why">The empress who seized a throne and an age and gave Russia both.</span></span></a></li></ol>
